From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Chulo <cchulo.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:27:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ASoC: amd: acp-config: ignore acp-audio-config-flag on
 ASUS RC74XA

The ASUS ROG Xbox Ally X20 (board RC74XA, ACP 7.0) BIOS reports
acp-audio-config-flag = 0x10 (FLAG_AMD_LEGACY_ONLY_DMIC) in the ACP
device _DSD. For ACP >= 7.0, snd_amd_acp_find_config() returns that
value as-is unless the board is in acp70_acpi_flag_override_table, and
snd_pci_ps (sound/soc/amd/ps/pci-ps.c) refuses to probe when the flag
is non-zero. The SoundWire links carrying the two TAS2783 amps (link 0)
and the RT721 (link 1) are then never scanned; only the legacy DMIC
driver binds. Windows ignores the flag.

Add the board to acp70_acpi_flag_override_table, the existing
dmi_check_system() table used for other ACP 7.0 machines with the same
BIOS problem, so the flag is treated as 0 and snd_pci_ps probes. The
legacy (snd-acp-pci) and SOF (snd-sof-amd-acp70) drivers keep backing
off, as they only accept the LEGACY/SOF flag values.

This is the in-kernel alternative to the early-initrd ACPI table
override that clears the flag in the DSDT. It changes
snd-acp-config.ko only and needs patch 0001 (machine layout) to get
speakers.

The match is on board vendor "ASUSTeK COMPUTER INC." and board name
"RC74XA" (DMI_MATCH, substring), as in Valve's kernel; the hunk is
byte-identical to it, and applied to v7.2.7 the file has git blob
45c7501851841a4d6a3eb88e4efcb4eb06e01ee4, the same as Valve's
7.2.10-valve1.

Derived from:
  - Valve linux-integration (mirror github.com/evlaV/linux-integration),
    commit 045b13e03d29 "[FOR-UPSTREAM] ASoC: amd: acp-config: force
    SoundWire probe on ASUS RC74XA" by Matthew Schwartz, in tag
    7.2.10-valve1
  - ovenham/rog-ally-x20-steamos-speaker-qam-fix,
    upstream/acp-config-rog-xbox-ally-x20.patch (proposed quirk,
    matches DMI_PRODUCT_NAME "RC74XA" instead)
  - anatase-org/kernel-anatase release 7.2.7-an22, patch-2-anatase.patch
  - stoneharborent/aquarius-os PR #40,
    build_files/x20-audio/rc74xa-acp-config.patch (DMI_EXACT_MATCH on
    the same board vendor/name)
  - hungarianhc/rog-ally-x20-steamos-speakers, README.md and
    ally-audio-fix.sh (diagnosis of the 0x10 flag; initrd override)

Validated with "git apply --check" against linux-stable v7.2.7 and
Valve 7.2.7-valve2 (the file is byte-identical in both, blob
8e1563824a97). Not compiled or run on hardware by this project yet.
---
 sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
index 8e1563824..45c750185 100644
--- a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
@@ -63,6 +63,13 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id acp70_acpi_flag_override_table[] = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "Vivobook 18 M1807GA"),
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		/* ASUS ROG Xbox Ally X20 (Strix Point, ACP 7.0) */
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "ASUSTeK COMPUTER INC."),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "RC74XA"),
+		},
+	},
 	{}
 };
 
